{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"40c7bceffc3a8768e20a5b4a9b80a0340cce1ef36be89599748cc9768cd2ba28","digest":{"component_or_area":"logging configuration (configure_logging)","key_entities":["src/rebar/review_bot/config.py:configure_logging()","src/rebar/review_bot/config.py:120","src/rebar/review_bot/config.py:145-146","logging.getLogger(\"rebar\")","lg.propagate","tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py::test_success_telemetry_survives_an_empty_usage_dict","tests/unit/test_review_bot.py:1288","src/rebar/review_bot/app.py:202","caplog","_pytest.logging.catching_logs"],"problem_keywords":["logging","caplog","propagation","test isolation","order-dependent failure","pytest"],"propositions":["configure_logging() sets propagate=False on the shared 'rebar' logger process-globally without restoration, blocking caplog from capturing any rebar.* logger records in subsequent tests","caplog assertions on rebar.* loggers silently fail (empty record lists) after configure_logging() has run in the same process, producing order-dependent test failures that are intermittent and non-local","the propagate=False was introduced to prevent double-logging through uvicorn/root in containers, but uvicorn does not add root handlers so propagation is safe and the marker-guarded handler alone prevents duplicates","removing the propagate=False mutation fixes the caplog capture while maintaining idempotent single-emission of log records and preserving existing test coverage"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787344952757908001,"uuid":"3ac91734-aa4f-4091-90e1-36888fde35b7"}